#
# What one form of capital shows as held, in minor units, in Sutra
# (ninefold_model.h NF2): the form's holder balances summed (minor) when
# the form is priceable (0 .. 3 and 8), and 0 for a state-reserved form
# (4 .. 7: social, natural, cultural, spiritual), which is never priced.
# form fits 9(1) and form + 1 must too, so a form past 8 is a size error,
# refused; minor fits 9(18), so a negative or a sum past 18 digits is
# refused. holding.tb says the same in Trebago, which answers both.
record form-holding
  form: 9(1)
  minor: 9(18)
  edge: 9(1)
procedure
  compute edge = form + 1
  if form >= 4 and form <= 7
    answer 0
  end-if
  answer minor
